                        "form": "фантазёрах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0d777e25-52d2-3eba-9c15-2da1a7f47281",
                        "entry_id": "a269390a-a895-33b0-a072-ab685a5eb2f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неодобр. человек, склонный фантазировать, мечтатель, строящий несбыточные планы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b12ada2e-bdad-4cf5-a607-013f5fe01b3b",
                                "sense_id": "0d777e25-52d2-3eba-9c15-2da1a7f47281",
                                "text": "Он женился в странной надежде, что тысяча рублей, которые были у его жены, помогут ему стать на ноги. Он поступил как фантазёр, как поэт, да так он и всегда поступал в жизни."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a216c8cf-baaf-4fd5-bff3-564934969a87",
                                "sense_id": "0d777e25-52d2-3eba-9c15-2da1a7f47281",
                                "text": "Русские бабы обязаны быть особенно консервативными, потому что в России мужчина ― фантазёр, мечтатель."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c410340-f7bb-4bc7-9a73-9e367586a571",
                        "source_entry_id": "a269390a-a895-33b0-a072-ab685a5eb2f2",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d777e25-52d2-3eba-9c15-2da1a7f47281",
                        "target_lang_word": "dreamer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dreamer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0a1f748-12d4-33f6-9430-ef5103a818f6",
                                        "entry_id": "cf53cebd-cd45-3224-9ff3-02e31eb86541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who dreams."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52baab2a-2010-3ab6-917c-1ecd9124d076",
                                        "entry_id": "cf53cebd-cd45-3224-9ff3-02e31eb86541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone whose beliefs are far from realistic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d1056ed-c47b-4b51-bb73-85280ee48223",
                                                "sense_id": "52baab2a-2010-3ab6-917c-1ecd9124d076",
                                                "text": "You may say I'm a dreamer/ But I'm not the only one/ I hope someday you'll join us/ And the world will live as one."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04604152-0ac9-4db0-9913-12dda52c2b16",
                                                "sense_id": "52baab2a-2010-3ab6-917c-1ecd9124d076",
                                                "text": "Eighties witches were not the patchouli-dipped, lovebead-wearing, back-to-the-earth dreamers of the seventies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b53a85e-0d63-3367-b9a8-108ec3c31e22",
                                        "entry_id": "cf53cebd-cd45-3224-9ff3-02e31eb86541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any anglerfish of the family Oneirodidae."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "828929e5-a0ab-39c4-b3bc-3b548489e2c4",
                                        "entry_id": "cf53cebd-cd45-3224-9ff3-02e31eb86541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A swallow-winged puffbird (Chelidoptera tenebrosa)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "16d896cd-4362-4db6-b5bf-fe011ec4d1da",
                        "source_entry_id": "a269390a-a895-33b0-a072-ab685a5eb2f2",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d777e25-52d2-3eba-9c15-2da1a7f47281",
                        "target_lang_word": "romancer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "romancer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "099256da-4b37-338b-a82b-486b2c0453ce",
                                        "entry_id": "0470753b-0ce1-313d-8ce5-501ad3a4a1a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who romances another; one who attempt to win another's affections via romance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7bc7abd-e672-4b61-8fd6-5b64bed52678",
                                                "sense_id": "099256da-4b37-338b-a82b-486b2c0453ce",
                                                "text": "Once I used to believe I was such a great romancer / then I came home to a woman that I did not recognize."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "216d70d8-77d7-3b47-af5c-dea90a4de72b",
                                        "entry_id": "0470753b-0ce1-313d-8ce5-501ad3a4a1a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who writes romance or adventure stories, especially stories relating to chivalry, knights, heroes, quests, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbfb796e-1c9c-42fd-ad31-5027bc813b40",
                                                "sense_id": "216d70d8-77d7-3b47-af5c-dea90a4de72b",
                                                "text": "[W]hat was once taught by sages, and believed by monarchs, has shared the fate of everything human and has sunk from its pristine rank to become the material and the machinery of poets and romancers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5cafa1c-1d6c-42b0-8550-e5571859ae23",
                                                "sense_id": "216d70d8-77d7-3b47-af5c-dea90a4de72b",
                                                "text": "No nightmare dreamed by man, no wild invention of the romancer, can ever equal the living horror of that place, and the weird crying of those voices of the night, as we clung like shipwrecked mariners to a raft, and tossed on the black, unfathomed wilderness of air."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "romancer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "064cfdcb-f34f-32a2-b35c-34162376bf95",
                                        "entry_id": "a13808b9-1dd0-3b9c-8ddc-4fb043f83928",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A romantic film or television show."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6639cc2-4917-472c-b6d7-259c38aef755",
                                                "sense_id": "064cfdcb-f34f-32a2-b35c-34162376bf95",
                                                "text": "Barbara Cartland scratched out this trusty 19th-century romancer concerning the scrumptious Serena Staverly (Diana Rigg), who has the dreadful misfortune to be lost in a game of cards to the flint-hearted Lord Justin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ef0c205e-9252-4fb7-ae81-44c7c5f90920",
                        "source_entry_id": "a269390a-a895-33b0-a072-ab685a5eb2f2",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d777e25-52d2-3eba-9c15-2da1a7f47281",
                        "target_lang_word": "make-believe",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "make-believe",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d554ab4d-802a-3d52-89d6-7207f4582ff0",
                                        "entry_id": "cf96860f-c7ef-339a-8cb6-a0673e7896cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or act of pretending; acting as if something is true when in fact one knows it is not."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "childish",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "563b24db-4985-424e-9c31-a40a686aec96",
                                                "sense_id": "d554ab4d-802a-3d52-89d6-7207f4582ff0",
                                                "text": "Come on, come on, I go up and down / I like this curious feeling / I know, I see, it's like make believe / Cover your ears so you can hear what I'm saying"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "922ca9ea-c932-3f3b-bd9a-2fd56ead0a78",
                                        "entry_id": "cf96860f-c7ef-339a-8cb6-a0673e7896cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of pretending or imagining that things are better than they really are."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "childish",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fc78d41-9369-364b-a0f8-44e22e0d09f7",
                                        "entry_id": "cf96860f-c7ef-339a-8cb6-a0673e7896cb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something imaginary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "childish",
                                            "countable",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f20c02b4-b9cf-44f0-b90d-9a1c8c440893",
                                                "sense_id": "3fc78d41-9369-364b-a0f8-44e22e0d09f7",
                                                "text": "‘You ought to be ashamed of yourself, Marjorie Lindon, to even think such nonsense. Are you all nerves and morbid imaginings,—you who have prided yourself on being so strong-minded! A pretty sort you are to do battle for anyone.—Why, they’re only make-believes!’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "make-believe",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b5a7010-dc0b-39bf-b866-cd540e5e5e41",
                                        "entry_id": "4793887f-3c12-3a5d-85ef-9fcc8397011c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Imaginary; not real; pretend."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "childish",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f402c286-d41e-46a1-a734-c78be9600cf4",
                                                "sense_id": "5b5a7010-dc0b-39bf-b866-cd540e5e5e41",
                                                "text": "He called himself Lord So-and-So, even had his family crest on the wall, but it was all totally make-believe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
